{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-1610"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Sawmilling and planing of wood"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "1610"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :wood-products/sawmilling
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :local-economy :resource-efficiency]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :sawmill-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :telemetry]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "SawmillAdvisor ⊣ Sawmill Plant Operations Governor, langgraph-clj
 StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS COORDINATION
 actor for sawmilling/planing (saws, planers, kilns) -- not direct
 saw/planer-equipment operation authority. Four ops
 (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` / `:flag-safety-
 concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect :propose` only. Ten
 concrete governor checks elaborate this blueprint's four HARD
 invariants: propose-only effect, closed op allowlist, closed
 proposal-effect allowlist (no direct saw/planer-equipment control),
 permanent kiln-schedule-finalize block, independent equipment
 verification/registration before maintenance scheduling, independent
 batch verification/registration before shipment coordination,
 independent shipment-volume recompute against the batch's own logged
 volume, double-schedule guard, lumber-grade validation, and
 moisture-content plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging
 ALWAYS escalates to a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch`
 is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when
 governor-clean."}
